---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy" description="GDPR and Uganda DPPA-compliant Privacy Policy for Yield Force, operated by Gaia Holdings Limited, incorporated in Uganda. Learn how we handle customer data, merchant integrations, AI processing, and sub-processors.">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mb-12 border-b border-slate-800 pb-8">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-blue-500/30 bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-400 text-xs font-medium mb-4">
        EU GDPR &amp; Uganda DPPA Compliance
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight mb-3">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
        Effective date: <span class="text-slate-300 font-medium">22 September 2026</span> · Last updated: <span class="text-slate-300 font-medium">22 September 2026</span>
      </p>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-2">
        <strong class="text-slate-400">Yield Force</strong> is a trading name of <strong class="text-slate-400">Gaia Holdings Limited</strong>, a company incorporated and registered in Uganda.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none text-slate-300 space-y-10 text-sm leading-relaxed">

      <!-- 1. Who We Are -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">1. Who We Are and How to Contact Us</h2>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Data Controller (for merchant accounts and website visitors):</p>
          <div class="bg-slate-900/60 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-800 text-xs space-y-1 text-slate-300">
            <p><strong class="text-white">Gaia Holdings Limited</strong> (trading as Yield Force)</p>
            <p>Incorporated in Uganda under the Companies Act, 2012</p>
            <p>Registration Number: [URSB Company Number]</p>
            <p>Privacy enquiries: <a href="mailto:privacy@yieldforce.dev" class="text-blue-400 hover:underline">privacy@yieldforce.dev</a></p>
            <p>Website: <a href="https://yieldforce.dev" class="text-blue-400 hover:underline">https://yieldforce.dev</a></p>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Netherlands Establishment (EU Operations):</p>
          <div class="bg-slate-900/60 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-800 text-xs space-y-1 text-slate-300">
            <p><strong class="text-white">Yield Force — Netherlands Office</strong></p>
            <p>[Street Address], [City], Netherlands</p>
            <p>Chamber of Commerce (KvK) Number: [KvK Number]</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 2. Regulatory Framework -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">2. Regulatory Framework</h2>
        <p>Gaia Holdings Limited is subject to two data protection regimes, both of which apply to our operations:</p>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">2.1 EU GDPR — Direct Application</h3>
          <p>Because we maintain a commercial establishment in the Netherlands, the <strong class="text-white">EU General Data Protection Regulation (Regulation (EU) 2016/679 — GDPR)</strong> applies directly to our processing activities under <strong class="text-white">Article 3(1) GDPR</strong> (<em>in the context of the activities of an establishment in the Union</em>). Our lead EU supervisory authority is the <strong class="text-white">Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens (AP)</strong> in the Netherlands.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">2.2 Uganda Data Protection and Privacy Act 2019 (DPPA)</h3>
          <p>As a company incorporated in Uganda, we are also bound by the <strong class="text-white">Data Protection and Privacy Act, 2019 (Act No. 9 of 2019, Cap. 97)</strong> and the <strong class="text-white">Data Protection and Privacy Regulations, 2021 (SI No. 84 of 2021)</strong>, supervised by the <strong class="text-white">Personal Data Protection Office (PDPO)</strong> under NITA-U.</p>
          <p>We are registered with the PDPO. Registration reference: [PDPO Registration Number].</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 3. Roles -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">3. Our Roles Under GDPR and the DPPA</h2>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="min-w-full text-left border border-slate-800 rounded-xl overflow-hidden text-xs">
            <thead class="bg-slate-900/80 text-slate-300 border-b border-slate-800">
              <tr>
                <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Processing Context</th>
                <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Our Role</th>
                <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Data Subjects</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800/60 bg-slate-900/30">
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3">Merchant registration, billing, platform accounts</td>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Data Controller</td>
                <td class="p-3">Merchant staff, account admins</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3">Website visitors, contact/demo enquiries</td>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Data Controller</td>
                <td class="p-3">Site visitors, prospective clients</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3">End-customer messaging (WhatsApp, Instagram, Facebook)</td>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Data Processor</td>
                <td class="p-3">Shoppers communicating with Shopify merchants</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>When we act as a <strong class="text-white">Data Processor</strong>, we process end-customer conversation data strictly on the documented instructions of the Shopify merchant (the Data Controller), pursuant to a GDPR Article 28 Data Processing Addendum (DPA).</p>
        <div class="bg-blue-900/20 border border-blue-700/30 rounded-xl p-4 text-slate-300 text-xs leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="text-white">Are you an end-customer?</strong> If you are a shopper who has chatted with an online store powered by Yield Force, the merchant operating that store is your Data Controller. To exercise your data protection rights, please contact that merchant directly. Where requests are submitted to us, we will promptly assist the merchant in fulfilling them in accordance with our DPA.
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 4. Data We Collect -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">4. Data We Collect as a Data Controller</h2>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">4.1 Merchant Account and Registration Data</h3>
          <p>When a Shopify merchant registers for Yield Force, we collect:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li><strong class="text-white">Identity data:</strong> Full name, business name, Shopify store URL, country.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Contact data:</strong> Business email address, support contact details.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Billing data:</strong> Subscription tier, billing address, VAT/tax identification number. Raw payment card details are processed exclusively by our payment processor (Stripe Payments Europe, Ltd.) under PCI-DSS Level 1 standards; Yield Force does not store card numbers.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Credential vault data:</strong> WhatsApp Business Account (WABA) IDs, Phone Number IDs, Meta System User Tokens, and Shopify API access tokens — stored in an encrypted, per-tenant credential vault using a Bring-Your-Own-Key (BYOK) architecture.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Technical and security logs:</strong> IP addresses, browser user-agent strings, login timestamps, API call logs.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">4.2 Website Visitor Data</h3>
          <p>When you visit <a href="https://yieldforce.dev" class="text-blue-400 hover:underline">yieldforce.dev</a>, we may collect:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li><strong class="text-white">Contact form submissions:</strong> Name, business email, message content.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Technical data:</strong> Server access logs (IP address, referrer, page path, timestamp) retained for security purposes. We do <strong class="text-white">not</strong> deploy analytics trackers, marketing pixels, or behavioural cookies.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 5. How We Use Your Data -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">5. How We Use Your Data and Our Legal Bases</h2>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">5.1 Under EU GDPR (Article 6)</h3>
          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="min-w-full text-left border border-slate-800 rounded-xl overflow-hidden text-xs">
              <thead class="bg-slate-900/80 text-slate-300 border-b border-slate-800">
                <tr>
                  <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Purpose</th>
                  <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Data Used</th>
                  <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Lawful Basis</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800/60 bg-slate-900/30">
                <tr><td class="p-3">Providing and administering the SaaS platform</td><td class="p-3">Merchant account data, credential vault data</td><td class="p-3 text-white font-medium">Art. 6(1)(b) — Performance of contract</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-3">Processing payments and issuing invoices</td><td class="p-3">Billing data, tax numbers</td><td class="p-3 text-white font-medium">Art. 6(1)(b); Art. 6(1)(c) — Legal obligation</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-3">Compliance with tax and legal obligations</td><td class="p-3">Financial records</td><td class="p-3 text-white font-medium">Art. 6(1)(c) — Legal obligation</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-3">Platform security, fraud detection, abuse prevention</td><td class="p-3">Technical logs, IP data</td><td class="p-3 text-white font-medium">Art. 6(1)(f) — Legitimate interests</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-3">Responding to contact/demo requests</td><td class="p-3">Contact form data</td><td class="p-3 text-white font-medium">Art. 6(1)(f) — Legitimate interests</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-3">Notifying merchants of platform changes or new sub-processors</td><td class="p-3">Contact data</td><td class="p-3 text-white font-medium">Art. 6(1)(b) — Performance of contract</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">5.2 Under Uganda DPPA (Section 7)</h3>
          <p>Processing of personal data of Ugandan data subjects is based on:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li><strong class="text-white">Section 7(2)(b) DPPA:</strong> Contractual necessity — for performance of our service agreements with Ugandan merchant clients.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Section 7(2)(a) DPPA:</strong> Legal authorisation — where processing is required or authorised by Ugandan law.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Section 7(1) DPPA:</strong> Informed consent — where none of the above grounds apply.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 6. AI and LLMs -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">6. Artificial Intelligence, LLMs, and Automated Decision-Making</h2>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">6.1 AI Models Used</h3>
          <p>Yield Force deploys Google Gemini Flash and Flash-Lite models to power intent classification, natural language response generation, sentiment analysis, and escalation detection.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">6.2 No Training on Customer Data</h3>
          <div class="bg-emerald-900/20 border border-emerald-700/30 rounded-xl p-4 text-slate-300 text-xs leading-relaxed">
            <strong class="text-white">Your personal data and customer message transcripts are processed strictly for real-time inference and workflow automation. Customer data is never used to train, retrain, or fine-tune any public or third-party foundation model.</strong> No customer data is shared with AI vendors for training purposes.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">6.3 GDPR Article 22 — Automated Decision-Making</h3>
          <p>Yield Force's AI engine assists merchants with automated conversational routing and draft response generation. <strong class="text-white">It does not make automated decisions that produce legal effects or similarly significantly affect individuals</strong> within the meaning of GDPR Article 22(1). Merchant administrators retain full supervisory control and override capability over all automated outputs via the Zone 5 Governance Portal.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 7. Processor Role -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">7. Data We Process as a Data Processor (End-Customer Conversations)</h2>
        <p>When merchants use Yield Force to power their customer messaging channels, we process end-customer data on the merchant's behalf as a Data Processor (GDPR Art. 28; DPPA s.2). This includes:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Platform-scoped user identifiers (WhatsApp phone numbers, Instagram Scoped User IDs, Facebook Page-Scoped IDs);</li>
          <li>Message content — customer inquiries, order queries, support requests;</li>
          <li>Message metadata — timestamps, delivery receipts, read receipts.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>All such processing is governed by a <strong class="text-white">Data Processing Addendum (DPA)</strong> between Yield Force and the merchant. Merchants may request a copy of our standard DPA at <a href="mailto:privacy@yieldforce.dev" class="text-blue-400 hover:underline">privacy@yieldforce.dev</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- 8. Sub-processors -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">8. Sub-processors</h2>
        <p>We engage the following sub-processors, each bound by equivalent data protection obligations (GDPR Art. 28(2)–(4); DPPA s.19):</p>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="min-w-full text-left border border-slate-800 rounded-xl overflow-hidden text-xs">
            <thead class="bg-slate-900/80 text-slate-300 border-b border-slate-800">
              <tr>
                <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Sub-processor</th>
                <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Location</th>
                <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Purpose</th>
                <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Transfer Mechanism</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800/60 bg-slate-900/30">
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white whitespace-nowrap">Supabase, Inc.</td>
                <td class="p-3">EU/EEA (Frankfurt)</td>
                <td class="p-3">Database hosting, authentication, row-level tenant isolation</td>
                <td class="p-3">EU data residency; SCCs where applicable</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white whitespace-nowrap">EU VPS Provider</td>
                <td class="p-3">EU/EEA</td>
                <td class="p-3">Application hosting and compute</td>
                <td class="p-3">EU data residency</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white whitespace-nowrap">Meta Platforms Ireland Limited</td>
                <td class="p-3">Ireland (EU)</td>
                <td class="p-3">WhatsApp Cloud API, Instagram Messaging API, Facebook Messenger API</td>
                <td class="p-3">EU establishment; Meta Business Platform Terms &amp; DPA</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white whitespace-nowrap">Shopify Inc.</td>
                <td class="p-3">Canada / global</td>
                <td class="p-3">Store API and webhook synchronisation</td>
                <td class="p-3">EU SCCs (Module 2)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white whitespace-nowrap">Stripe Payments Europe, Ltd.</td>
                <td class="p-3">Ireland (EU)</td>
                <td class="p-3">Merchant subscription billing</td>
                <td class="p-3">EU establishment</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white whitespace-nowrap">Google LLC (Gemini API)</td>
                <td class="p-3">USA</td>
                <td class="p-3">AI inference — zero customer data retained for training</td>
                <td class="p-3">EU SCCs (Module 2) + TIA</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>We will provide at least <strong class="text-white">14 days' written notice</strong> before adding any new sub-processor.</p>
        <div class="bg-slate-900/60 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-800 text-xs text-slate-400">
          <strong class="text-slate-300">Meta API note:</strong> When you interact with a merchant via WhatsApp, Instagram, or Facebook Messenger, your messages are transmitted through Meta Platforms Ireland Limited (4 Grand Canal Square, Grand Canal Harbour, Dublin 2, Ireland). Yield Force does not access your personal Meta account credentials; all interactions occur via authorised business webhooks.
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 9. International Transfers -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">9. International Data Transfers</h2>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">9.1 Netherlands (EU) → Uganda</h3>
          <p>Uganda has <strong class="text-white">not</strong> received an adequacy decision from the European Commission (GDPR Art. 45). Transfers of EU personal data to Gaia Holdings Limited in Uganda are therefore governed by:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li><strong class="text-white">EU Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs)</strong> — Commission Implementing Decision (EU) 2021/914, Module 2 (Controller-to-Processor) or Module 1 (Controller-to-Controller) as applicable; and</li>
            <li>A documented <strong class="text-white">Transfer Impact Assessment (TIA)</strong> in accordance with <em>Schrems II</em> (Case C-311/18) and EDPB Recommendations 01/2020, including encryption in transit (TLS 1.3) and at rest (AES-256), with cryptographic keys managed within the EU or by an independent EU custodian.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">9.2 Uganda → Netherlands (EU)</h3>
          <p>Transfers of personal data from Uganda to the Netherlands are authorised under <strong class="text-white">Section 19(a) of the DPPA 2019</strong>, on the basis that the Netherlands (as an EU Member State subject to the GDPR and UAVG) provides data protection standards that meet or exceed those of the DPPA. We maintain a documented adequacy assessment on file for PDPO inspection purposes (DPPR Reg. 30(5)).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">9.3 Core EU Data Residency</h3>
          <p>All primary databases, conversation logs, and tenant configurations are stored within EU/EEA data centres (Supabase Frankfurt region). Cross-border processing to Uganda consists primarily of operational access for platform administration, subject to the safeguards in §9.1.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 10. Security -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">10. Security Measures (GDPR Article 32; DPPA Section 20)</h2>
        <p>We implement the following technical and organisational measures:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li><strong class="text-white">Encryption in transit:</strong> TLS 1.3 for all data in motion.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">Encryption at rest:</strong> AES-256 for all database storage.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">Tenant isolation:</strong> Per-tenant Sovereign Key and Supabase Row-Level Security (RLS) — no cross-tenant data access is architecturally possible.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">Credential security:</strong> BYOK vault — merchant API keys and Meta System User Tokens are encrypted per-tenant.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">Webhook security:</strong> HMAC-SHA256 signature verification for all Meta and Shopify webhook payloads.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">Access control:</strong> Role-based access control (RBAC) on a least-privilege basis.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">Data breach response:</strong> We will notify the <strong class="text-white">AP</strong> within <strong class="text-white">72 hours</strong> of confirming a personal data breach (GDPR Art. 33); we will notify the <strong class="text-white">PDPO</strong> immediately upon becoming aware of a security breach (DPPA s.21); affected data subjects will be notified without undue delay where required.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- 11. Retention -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">11. Data Retention</h2>
        <p>We retain personal data only for as long as necessary for the stated purposes:</p>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="min-w-full text-left border border-slate-800 rounded-xl overflow-hidden text-xs">
            <thead class="bg-slate-900/80 text-slate-300 border-b border-slate-800">
              <tr>
                <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Data Category</th>
                <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Retention Period</th>
                <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Basis</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800/60 bg-slate-900/30">
              <tr><td class="p-3">Merchant account and profile data</td><td class="p-3">Duration of active contract + 90 days</td><td class="p-3">Contract performance; post-cancellation export window</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3">End-customer chat transcripts</td><td class="p-3">30–90 days (merchant-configurable)</td><td class="p-3">Processor instructions under DPA</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3">Webhook ingest and API logs</td><td class="p-3">14–30 days (rolling)</td><td class="p-3">Legitimate interests — security and debugging</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3">Encrypted database backups</td><td class="p-3">Rolling 14–30 days</td><td class="p-3">Disaster recovery</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3">Financial, billing, and tax records</td><td class="p-3"><strong class="text-white">5 years</strong> from end of tax period</td><td class="p-3">Legal obligation — Uganda Tax Procedures Code Act 2014 (s.15); Uganda Companies Act 2012 (s.147)</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3">Customer erasure requests (<code class="text-blue-300">customers/redact</code>)</td><td class="p-3">Purged within 30 days of receipt</td><td class="p-3">GDPR Art. 17; DPPA s.23; Shopify Partner requirements</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="p-3">Shop erasure on uninstall (<code class="text-blue-300">shop/redact</code>)</td><td class="p-3">Purged within 30 days of uninstall</td><td class="p-3">GDPR Art. 17; DPPA s.23; Shopify Partner requirements</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 12. Your Rights -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">12. Your Rights</h2>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200">12.1 Rights Under EU GDPR (Articles 15–22) — EU/EEA Data Subjects</h3>
          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="min-w-full text-left border border-slate-800 rounded-xl overflow-hidden text-xs">
              <thead class="bg-slate-900/80 text-slate-300 border-b border-slate-800">
                <tr>
                  <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Right</th>
                  <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">What It Means</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800/60 bg-slate-900/30">
                <tr><td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Access (Art. 15)</td><td class="p-3">Request a copy of personal data we hold about you</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Rectification (Art. 16)</td><td class="p-3">Request correction of inaccurate or incomplete data</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Erasure (Art. 17)</td><td class="p-3">Request deletion where grounds apply</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Restriction (Art. 18)</td><td class="p-3">Request suspension of processing pending a dispute</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Data Portability (Art. 20)</td><td class="p-3">Receive your data in a machine-readable format (JSON/CSV)</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Object (Art. 21)</td><td class="p-3">Object to processing based on legitimate interests</td></tr>
